From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 19:15:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 56/59] fix(gauntlet-tdd): route the note-write guard's own bd
 match through gc (gcp-dnxq)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The `--notes` guard added in 25a61a8 filtered candidate lines on the bare
substring `"bd update"`, which trips the repo's own bare-bd guard
(tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py) — that scanner reads the literal as a
shipped asset invoking `bd` outside store-aware routing.

Matching on `"gc bd update"` clears the scanner and is the more precise
filter besides: every note write in the formula is `gc bd`-routed, so a
line that reaches the assertion via the bare form would already be a
different violation.

`pytest tests/test_no_bare_bd_commands.py gauntlet-tdd/tests` -> 23 passed,
51 subtests passed. Reintroducing the --notes regression still fails both
NoteWritesAppendTests guards; restoring the fix passes both.
---
 gauntlet-tdd/tests/test_gauntlet_tdd_formulas.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gauntlet-tdd/tests/test_gauntlet_tdd_formulas.py b/gauntlet-tdd/tests/test_gauntlet_tdd_formulas.py
index 886b5a1..41b7002 100644
--- a/gauntlet-tdd/tests/test_gauntlet_tdd_formulas.py
+++ b/gauntlet-tdd/tests/test_gauntlet_tdd_formulas.py
@@ -368,7 +368,7 @@ class NoteWritesAppendTests(unittest.TestCase):
             data = tomllib.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
             for step_id, body in step_bodies(data).items():
                 for line in shell_lines(body):
-                    if "bd update" not in line:
+                    if "gc bd update" not in line:
                         continue
                     with self.subTest(formula=path.name, step=step_id, line=line):
                         self.assertIsNone(
